# Config files

- YAML config files for individual runs or sweeps are stored in configs/ or subfolders therein.
- Config files are artefacts that must be preserved to ensure the reproducibility of experiments.
- Never modify an existing config file unless specifically instructed to do so or unless you generated the config file yourself. Instead, make a copy with a descriptive name and work on the copy.
- In addition, never delete or modify any file that has "backup" in its name.
